.TH PROVIUM 1 "" "Provium 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
provium \- Run Lua Tests against Virtual Machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B provium
.RI [ options ]\ [ paths ...]\ [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Provium discovers files ending in .test.lua and runs each in its own Lua
state. Tests within a file run sequentially. The dispatcher can run several
files together, subject to their memory and CPU claims.
.PP
Positional paths select test discovery roots. Without paths, discovery
starts in the current directory. The roots setting in provium.toml supplies
helper and fixture search paths; it does not replace positional paths.
.PP
The qemu backend starts guests using the configured kernel and initrd.
It needs QEMU, KVM, vsock, and the host network tools and access checked by
preflight. The local backend runs agent operations on the host and does not
qualify a guest kernel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-config " PATH"
Read PATH instead of ./provium.toml.
.TP
.BR \-filter " TEXT"
Select files whose discovered relative path contains TEXT.
.TP
.BR \-tag " TAG"
Select tests with a matching tag. Repeated values are alternatives.
.TP
.BR \-no-tag " TAG"
Exclude tests with a matching tag. Exclusions take precedence.
.TP
.BR \-tag-meta " KEY=VALUE"
Select metadata values. Repeated values for one key are alternatives;
different keys must all match.
.TP
.BR \-no-tag-meta " KEY=VALUE"
Exclude matching metadata values, taking precedence over inclusion.
.TP
.B \-include-slow
Include tests marked slow.
.TP
.B \-rerun-failed
Restrict discovered files to the saved failure list.
.TP
.BR \-since " PATH"
Select files modified after PATH.
.TP
.B \-watch
Poll for changes every 500 milliseconds and repeat the run.
.TP
.B \-fail-fast
Stop dispatch after the first failed file.
.TP
.BR \-timeout " DURATION"
Set the per-file execution timeout. The default is 300 seconds. Accepts
integer seconds or duration suffixes such as 500ms, 30s, 10m, and 2h.
Zero turns the file timeout off. Queue time is not counted.
.TP
.BR \-mem " SIZE"
Set the pool memory budget in bytes or with a suffix such as 512M or 2G.
The default uses 80 percent of detected host memory.
.TP
.BR \-cpus " COUNT"
Set the pool CPU budget. The default uses the detected online CPU count.
.TP
.BR \-cpu-overcommit " FACTOR"
Multiply the CPU budget. The default is 1.0; the accepted value is clamped
to the range 0.5 through 8.0.
.TP
.BR \-vmm " qemu|local"
Select the backend. The default is qemu.
.TP
.B \-no-preflight
Skip startup capability checks. This does not provide missing capabilities.
.TP
.B \-no-ksm
Preserve host Kernel Same-page Merging settings instead of tuning them.
.TP
.B \-no-build
Skip automatic dynamic-profile build hooks during execution.
The prepare subcommand still runs builds.
.TP
.B \-json
Write one JSON result per file. Conflicts with \-events-stdout.
.TP
.BR \-save-events " PATH"
Save length-prefixed MessagePack events to PATH.
.TP
.B \-events-stdout
Write MessagePack events to standard output and human results to standard
error. Conflicts with \-json.
.TP
.BR \-events-socket " PATH"
Serve the live event stream on a Unix socket.
.TP
.B \-coverage
Run provium-coverage on the captured events after execution.
The consumer must be available on PATH.
.TP
.BR \-verbose , " \-quiet"
Show passing tests or restrict output to failures. These conflict.
The short forms are \-v and \-q.
.TP
.B \-no-progress
Suppress the interactive progress bar.
.TP
.BR \-help , " \-version"
Print help or the version. The short forms are \-h and \-V.
.SH COMMANDS
Global options and discovery paths precede the subcommand.
.TP
.B list [\-\-fixtures]
List discovered tests, or fixtures, without running them.
.TP
.B prepare [PROFILE]
Run a profile's build command, or all declared builds in name order.
Does not boot guests. A build failure stops preparation.
.TP
.B repl [PROFILE] [\-\-fixture NAME] [\-\-name NAME]
Start an interactive Lua session using a profile or cached fixture.
.TP
.B console PROFILE
Attach to a guest serial console. Options include \-mem SIZE, \-cpus COUNT,
\-\-cmdline TEXT, \-agent, \-qemu PATH, and \-print-command.
A double-hyphen separator introduces extra QEMU arguments.
.TP
.B fixture list
List cached entries.
.TP
.B fixture build NAME
Build a fixture if not already cached.
.TP
.B fixture rebuild NAME
Remove that fixture's cached entry and build it again.
.TP
.B fixture clean
Remove the fixture cache.
.TP
.B fixture stale
List fixtures whose source identity has no matching cache entry.
.TP
.B lsp-setup [DIR] [\-\-force]
Write Lua editor definitions and configuration. The default directory is
the current directory. Existing editor configuration requires an explicit
force option to overwrite.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PROVIUM_OVERLAY
Path to the matching static guest agent overlay.
.TP
.B PROVIUM_RERUN_STATE
Override the failure-list path, normally ~/.cache/provium/rerun.json.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B provium.toml
Profiles, fixture and helper roots, and cache settings.
.TP
.B ../share/provium/agent-overlay.cpio.gz
Overlay path relative to the installed executable's directory.
.TP
.B ~/.cache/provium/fixtures
Default fixture cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All selected tests passed or were skipped.
.TP
.B 1
At least one test file failed or timed out.
.TP
.B 2
A configuration, preflight, or infrastructure error prevented the run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR provium-coverage (1)
.PP
The Provium technical reference in Peios Learn describes Lua interfaces,
profile fields, wire versions, and resource ownership.
